    "title": "Man found stabbed to death in Fontana - NewsBreak",
    "text": "A suspect remains at large after a man was found stabbed to death in Fontana. On June 13, San Bernardino County deputies responded to an assault at a home on the 9000 Block of Hemlock Avenue around 3 p.m. Arriving deputies found the victim, Antonio Fonseca, 36, of Fontana, lying on the street near the property with stab wounds. He was pronounced dead at the scene. No suspect was found in the area. Several witnesses were questioned about the deadly stabbing, but no suspect was positively identified. No further details, including possible motive, were released. Anyone who may have witnessed the deadly stabbing or has information on the case is urged to call the San Bernardino County Sheriff’s Department at 909-890-4904. Anonymous tips can be provided to We-Tip at 1-800-782-7463 or online at wetip.com. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KTLA.",
